ours</a>` line.\n\n`home.spec.ts > home page > links to the opening hours` asserts `page.locator('a').getAttribute('href')` is `/hours`, and it is currently green. Leave that anchor exactly as it is: one single anchor element in the whole document, with `href` spelled as the root-relative `/hours` (not `hours`, not an absolute URL, not with a query string or trailing slash). This test also relies on strict-mode single resolution, so do not add any further `<a>` elements — no navigation bar, no footer links, no \"back\" link — while fixing the heading. This part of the plan is a do-not-break constraint rather than new work.\n\n### Part 3 — Refresh the now-stale source comments (serves no test; correctness of the file as left behind)\n\n**File:** `services/web/server.js` — the three-line comment at the top of the file.\n\nThe header comment currently announces the bug: it says the heading \"says `Welcome` where the store's name belongs: that is the planted defect, in PRODUCTION source, which the fix loop has to correct.\" Once Part 1 lands, that sentence describes code that no longer exists and would misdirect the next reader. Rewrite those lines to describe the file as it then is — a single-page HTML front for the Corner Shop, served on the port `PORT` names — and drop the planted-defect narration. Keep the first line's useful description of the service. Do not delete the whole comment block; a short accurate comment is better than none.\n\n## Explicitly out of scope\n\n- Do **not** touch `tests/integration/home.spec.ts`, `tests/playwright.config.ts`, `tests/package.json`, or anything else under `tests/`. The failing assertion is the specification; the expected string `Corner Shop` must stay exactly as written, and no assertion may be weakened, loosened to `toContain`/a regex, trimmed, retried via `expect.poll`, skipped, or annotated with `test.fail`/`test.fixme`.\n- Do **not** touch `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml`, `CLAUDE.md`, or `true-bdd/`. The architecture